Meesho Reseller Growth & Alert Intelligence Pipeline
Meesho's reseller-operations team tracks tens of thousands of individual resellers who list and sell products across categories such as ethnic wear, western wear, kids wear, home & kitchen, and beauty & personal care. Every month, category managers need to know which categories moved enough to matter, which resellers are inactive, and which regions are pulling their weight — without waiting for an analyst to manually rebuild the same spreadsheet from scratch. Today that monitoring is manual: someone opens last month's numbers, eyeballs the change, and drafts an update by hand. It is slow, inconsistent between analysts, and prone to exactly the kind of narrative errors — invented numbers, overstated claims, dropped caveats — that make leadership stop trusting a report.

Your task is to build a small, working, end-to-end reseller growth-monitoring pipeline for Meesho: a SQL layer that answers the team's standing business questions against a reseller/order dataset, a Python engine that turns "significant change" from a vague phrase into a numeric, testable rule with proper input validation, a reliable AI-narrative layer that turns verified numbers into a stakeholder-ready update without ever inventing a figure, and an agent specification (plus a working mock runner) that ties all three together into one repeatable, guarded, human-reviewed workflow — exactly the kind of system a reseller-ops analytics team would actually run every month.
